  "narrative": {
    "intro": "California has recorded $399M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 99.3% year over year. Award activity so far includes 3,231 awards with an average award size of $124K. Historical context shows much larger annual totals in recent years: FY22 recorded $57.5B, FY23 recorded $61.5B, FY24 recorded $61.7B, FY25 recorded $62B, and FY26 recorded $57.1B. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in FY2027 to date with $237M obligated. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration follows with $138M. CALIFORNIA INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date with $78.4M in obligations. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the largest industry sector in FY2027 to date with $91M in obligations. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial for the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with prior years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date shows $399M in obligations, compared with prior full fiscal years that ranged from $57.1B to $62B. Obligations fell 99.3% year over year. The contrast reflects that current-year totals are partial and earlier years represent full fiscal-year totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $237M, and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $138M. CALIFORNIA INSTITUTE OF TECHNOLOGY received $78.4M, and IMPULSE SPACE, INC. received $37.1M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences leads industries with $91M in obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
